BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Noir: The Man I Love (1946)
DTSTART:20260215T000000Z
DTEND:20260215T021500Z
DTSTAMP:20260215T000000Z
UID:NjpR41REOr
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 116 mins (1h56m)\n\nA coast-to-coast road trip throu
 gh a world of atmospheric nightclubs\, tenements\, and backlot streets\, 
 this majestic melodrama is part noir\, part soap opera\, and pure Hollywoo
 d magic. As flinty chanteuse Petey Brown\, Ida Lupino is at the apex of 
 her big-screen glamour.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/programs-and-events/noir-c
 ity/the-man-i-love\n\nEstimated start: 16:15
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Downtown\, 2100 4th Avenue
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Noir: Gilda (1946)
DTSTART:20260215T030000Z
DTEND:20260215T052500Z
DTSTAMP:20260215T030000Z
UID:KCWZ63oIob
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 130 mins (2h10m)\n\nThe sexual tension flies when Jo
 hnny Farrell (Glenn Ford) accepts a gig with sinister casino owner Ballin 
 Mundson (George Macready) only to reignite a romance with Mundson’s bomb
 shell wife\, Gilda (Rita Hayworth). Cue betrayal\, innuendo-spiked dialogu
 e\, and Hayworth’s legendary “Put the Blame on Mame” performance.\n\
 nhttps://www.siff.net/programs-and-events/noir-city/gilda\n\nEstimated sta
 rt: 19:15
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Downtown\, 2100 4th Avenue
END:VEVENT
